  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1986b61d-de03-46e7-bb43-1d9746374fdb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### CIs in Simple Linear Regression"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d1659ac4-74c3-4021-84f2-16e6b02103dd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "So far we've learned about CIs for our LS coefficients $\\hat{\\beta}_k,~k=0,1,$ and also for the mean of the response at given levels of the predictor $E(Y|X=x)$.\n",
    "\n",
    "They take the form: \n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\widehat{\\beta}_0 \\pm t^*_{n-2}(1-\\alpha/2)\\cdot  \\widehat{\\sigma}\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n} + \\frac{\\bar{x}^2}{SSX}}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\widehat{\\beta}_1 \\pm t^*_{n-2}(1-\\alpha/2) \\cdot \\widehat{\\sigma}\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{SSX}}$$\n",
    "and \n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\widehat{y} (x) \\pm t^*_{n-2}(1-\\alpha/2) \\cdot \\widehat{\\sigma}\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n} + \\frac{(x - \\bar{x})^2}{SSX}}.$$\n",
    "Also recall that the last term $\\widehat{y} (x)$ is an estimate of $g(x) = E(y|X = x)$, the mean of the response at a given $x$ value. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b36b0622-da52-40ed-8f43-89b731c72d87",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Notice the general form of each of these intervals is:\n",
    "$$estimate \\pm MoE  $$\n",
    "$$estimate \\pm crit. value \\cdot (typical~ prediction~ error)$$\n",
    "$$estimate \\pm crit. value \\cdot \\widehat{SE}(estimate - target)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "(MoE = margin of error)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6892d5b2-d357-4a50-a57e-94de273500a4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
